<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Korean War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1950–1953</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Korean War began on 25 June 1950 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-korea">North Korea</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a>. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> force led by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> drove the North back towards the Chinese border, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a> then intervened with massive forces. After the front stabilised near the 38th parallel, an armistice was signed in July 1953. The war turned occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> into a supply base and hardened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> divisions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/korean-war.jpg" alt="Korean War" width="320" height="257" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photo by Corporal Peter McDonald, USMC · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chosin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
